So `EVP_PKEY_assign_DH` is just `EVP_PKEY_assign(pkey, EVP_PKEY_DH, dh)`. Let me look at `EVP_PKEY_assign`:

```c
int EVP_PKEY_assign(EVP_PKEY *pkey, int type, void *key)
{
    ...
    if (pkey == NULL || !EVP_PKEY_set_type(pkey, type))
        return 0;
    if (!EVP_PKEY_set_alias_type(pkey, alias))
        return 0;
    pkey->pkey.ptr = key;
    return (key != NULL);
}
```

So after `EVP_PKEY_assign_DH(peer_tmp, dh)` succeeds, `peer_tmp->pkey.dh = dh`. The DH object is now owned by the EVP_PKEY.

Now look at the error path in `tls_process_ske_dhe`:
```c
err:
    BN_free(p);
    BN_free(g);
    BN_free(bnpub_key);
    DH_free(dh);       // <-- This frees dh
    EVP_PKEY_free(peer_tmp);  // <-- This also tries to free dh via evp_pkey_free_it -> pkey_free -> DH_free
```

This is a double-free! But wait, the crash is a use-after-free, not a double-free. Let me think about this more carefully.

Actually, looking at the code flow more carefully: when `ssl_security` fails, `dh` is still set (not NULL), and `peer_tmp` also owns `dh`. So `DH_free(dh)` will free the DH object, decrementing its reference count to 0 and freeing it. Then `EVP_PKEY_free(peer_tmp)` will call `evp_pkey_free_it(peer_tmp)` which calls `x->ameth->pkey_free(x)` which calls `DH_free(peer_tmp->pkey.dh)` again - a double free.

But the crash report says "Heap-use-after-free WRITE 4" in `CRYPTO_DOWN_REF`. Let me look at `DH_free` again:

```c
void DH_free(DH *r)
{
    int i;
    if (r == NULL)
        return;
    CRYPTO_DOWN_REF(&r->references, &i, r->lock);  // <-- This is the write
    ...
}
```

So the first `DH_free(dh)` frees the DH object. Then `EVP_PKEY_free(peer_tmp)` calls `evp_pkey_free_it` which calls `x->ameth->pkey_free(x)` which calls `DH_free(peer_tmp->pkey.dh)` which tries to access `r->references` which is already freed - use-after-free!

But wait, `EVP_PKEY_assign` sets `pkey->pkey.ptr = key` and `EVP_PKEY_set_type` calls `pkey_set_type` which calls `evp_pkey_free_it(pkey)` if `pkey->pkey.ptr` is not NULL. But `peer_tmp` is newly created, so `pkey->pkey.ptr` is NULL initially.

